{# O'Deadly Skyrim decision template. Context from Papyrus: actor_name, target_name, situation.
   Answer key read by the script: question "would" (noul) -> "true" / "false". #}
[ state actor ]
{% for n in get_nearby_npc_list(player.UUID) %}{% if decnpc(n.UUID).name == actor_name %}{{ render_character_profile("short_inline", n.UUID) }}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
Name: {{ actor_name }}
[ end state ]

[ state target ]
{% if target_name == decnpc(player.UUID).name %}{{ render_character_profile("short_inline", player.UUID) }}
{% else %}{% for n in get_nearby_npc_list(player.UUID) %}{% if decnpc(n.UUID).name == target_name %}{{ render_character_profile("short_inline", n.UUID) }}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
Name: {{ target_name }}
[ end state ]

[ state situation ]
{{ situation }}
[ end state ]

[ question would noul ]
In a harsh, lawless corner of Skyrim, would {{ actor_name }} force themselves on {{ target_name }} in this `situation`?
Judge only from who {{ actor_name }} is in `actor`: their temperament, morals, appetites, loyalties and how they regard {{ target_name }} (`target`).
Decent, loyal, timid or principled characters would not. Cruel, predatory, lustful, desperate or contemptuous characters might.
[ criteria ]
true: yes, this is something {{ actor_name }} would do here
false: no, {{ actor_name }} would not do this
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
